Refresh the fallback theme's cached palette when the portal color scheme changes.
Qt 6.11.3 receives Settings.SettingChanged and updates colorScheme(), but the
delegated system palette otherwise retains its startup colors. The native
requestColorScheme() hook invalidates that cache before handleThemeChange()
rebuilds the application palette.

Verified with Qt 6.11.3 Widgets on Wayland, including QProxyStyle as used by PCManFM-Qt.
Retest without this patch when updating Qt; remove it when upstream handles
fallback palette invalidation itself.

--- a/src/plugins/platformthemes/xdgdesktopportal/qxdgdesktopportaltheme.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platformthemes/xdgdesktopportal/qxdgdesktopportaltheme.cpp
@@ -75,6 +75,7 @@
         if (group == appearanceInterface) {
             if (key == colorSchemeKey) {
                 colorScheme = colorSchemeFromXdgPref(static_cast<XdgColorschemePref>(value.variant().toUInt()));
+                baseTheme->requestColorScheme(colorScheme);
                 QWindowSystemInterface::handleThemeChange();
             } else if (key == contrastKey) {
                 contrast = static_cast<Qt::ContrastPreference>(value.variant().toUInt());
